{# Sequence rail — this entry's position in the register, as navigation.
   Expects:
     seqNeighbours — array from the neighbourhood filter (oldest → newest,
                     current entry flagged)

   Encoding: one mark per entry on a hairline, older on the left. Type is
   shape and fill together: article = filled square, digesting = open square,
   project note = coral diamond. The current entry is a filled coral square.

   The key below the rail is not decoration. Without it the marks are an
   undocumented code -- some filled, some not, for reasons a reader can only
   discover by hovering each one in turn, which is not a thing anyone does.
   A datasheet states its legend; so does this.

   Every mark is a real link with the title and date in both the tooltip and
   visually-hidden text, so with CSS off this degrades to a plain list of
   nearby entries. That is also why the "Previously:" and "Next:" lines were
   dropped from the entry foot: they restated two of these marks in prose. #}
{%- if seqNeighbours and seqNeighbours.length > 1 -%}
<nav class="kh-seq" aria-label="Nearby entries in the register" data-pagefind-ignore>
  <p class="kh-meta kh-seq__caption"><span class="kh-seq__dir" aria-hidden="true">← older</span><span class="kh-seq__dir" aria-hidden="true">newer →</span></p>
  <ol class="kh-seq__track">
    {%- for n in seqNeighbours %}
    <li class="kh-seq__item">
      {%- if n.current %}
      <span class="kh-seq__mark kh-seq__mark--{{ n.type }} kh-seq__mark--current" title="{{ n.dateLabel }} — this entry" aria-current="page">
        <span class="kh-u-sr-only">This entry ({{ n.dateLabel }})</span>
      </span>
      {%- else %}
      <a class="kh-seq__mark kh-seq__mark--{{ n.type }}" href="{{ n.url | url }}" title="{{ n.dateLabel }} — {{ n.title }}">
        <span class="kh-u-sr-only">{{ n.title }} ({{ n.dateLabel }})</span>
      </a>
      {%- endif %}
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>

  {#- aria-hidden: the marks above already carry their type in their
      visually-hidden text, so reading the key aloud would only add noise. -#}
  <ul class="kh-seq__key" aria-hidden="true">
    <li class="kh-seq__key-item"><span class="kh-seq__mark kh-seq__mark--article kh-seq__mark--key"></span>Post</li>
    <li class="kh-seq__key-item"><span class="kh-seq__mark kh-seq__mark--digesting kh-seq__mark--key"></span>Digesting</li>
    <li class="kh-seq__key-item"><span class="kh-seq__mark kh-seq__mark--impact kh-seq__mark--key"></span>Project note</li>
    <li class="kh-seq__key-item"><span class="kh-seq__mark kh-seq__mark--article kh-seq__mark--current kh-seq__mark--key"></span>You are here</li>
  </ul>
</nav>
{%- endif -%}
